/volume><fpage>688</fpage><lpage>694</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000556-SchmidHempel1"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schmid-Hempel</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Schmid-Hempel</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Colony performance and immunocompetence of a social insect, <italic>Bombus terrestris</italic>, in poor and variable environments.</article-title><source>Funct Ecol</source><volume>12</volume><fpage>22</fpage><lpage>30</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000556-Ings1"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ings</surname><given-names>TC</given-names></name><name><surname>Ward</surname><given-names>NL</given-names></name><name><surname>Chittka</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Can commercially imported bumblebees out-compete their native conspecifics?</article-title><source>J Appl Ecol</source><volume>43</volume><fpage>940</fpage><lpage>948</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000556-Chittka4"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chittka</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Wells</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Color vision in bees: mechanisms, ecology and evolution.</article-title><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Prete</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><source>Complex Worlds from Simpler Nervous Systems</source><publisher-loc>Cambridge, USA</publisher-loc><publisher-name>MIT Press</publisher-name><fpage>165</fpage><lpage>191</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000556-Chittka5"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chittka</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Optimal sets of color receptors and color opponent systems for coding of natural objects in insect vision.</article-title><source>J Theor Biol</source><volume>181</volume><fpage>179</fpage><lpage>196</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000556-Ings2"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ings</surname><given-names>TC</given-names></name><name><surname>Schikora</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Chittka</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Bumblebees, humble pollinators or assiduous invaders? A population comparison of foraging performance in <italic>Bombus terrestris</italic>.</article-title><source>Oecologia</source><volume>144</volume><fpage>508</fpage><lpage>516</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15891827</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000556-Spaethe1"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Spaethe</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Weidenm&#x000fc;ller</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Size variation and foraging rate in bumblebees (<italic>Bombus terrestris</italic>).</article-title><source>Insect Soc</source><volume>49</volume><fpage>142</fpage><lpage>146</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000556-Allen1"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Allen</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Cameron</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>McGinley</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Heinrich</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><year>1978</year><article-title>The role of workers and new queens in the ergonomics of a bumblebee colony (Hymenoptera: Apoidea).</article-title><source>J Kans Entomol Soc</source><volume>51</volume><fpage>329</fpage><lpage>342</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000556-Raine2"><label>27</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Raine</surname><given-names>NE</given-names></name><name><surname>Chittka</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Nectar production rates of 75 bumblebee-visited flower species in a German flora (Hymenoptera: Apidae: <italic>Bombus terrestris</italic>).</article-title><source>Entomol Gen</source><comment>in press</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000556-Chittka6"><label>28</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chittka</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Kevan</surname><given-names>PG</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Flower colour as advertisement.</article-title><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Dafni</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Kevan</surname><given-names>PG</given-names></name><name><surname>Husband</surname><given-names>BC</given-names></name></person-group><source>Practical Pollination Biology</source><publisher-loc>Cambridge, Ontario</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Enviroquest Ltd</publisher-name><fpage>157</fpage><lpage>196</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000556-Rauh1"><label>29</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rauh</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Senghas</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><year>1987</year><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Fitschen</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><source>Flora von Deutschland und seinen angrenzenden Gebieten</source><publisher-loc>He